# Fixture for spec_library/block_model/native_codegen.feature (Phase 19).
# Confirms fiber_yield compiles and runs through REAL native codegen
# without crashing -- os_fiber_yield is a genuine, already-compiled
# x64_runtime.patlang primitive (real OS threads under the hood, per
# fiber_demo.patlang's own header). Full pause/resume semantics from
# OUTSIDE a natively-compiled process aren't exercised here: that needs
# fiber_new/fiber_resume also recognized as block-model calls, which
# this pass doesn't add -- named as a real, separate follow-up, not
# assumed covered by this smoke check.

make a function called start returns r
  fiber_yield(7)
  print(999)
end
